      "writtenOn": "2025-09-29T08:57:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A normal host will not do that as these memory pages are not freed back to the kernel yet, but a malicious host will indeed do that. So you are right, we should not writing anything after undonating it thus seems we will need a __noclear version for this case, as well as for teardown_donated_memory() case.",
      "parentUuid": "e0f46e4f_24b44134",
      "revId": "5871a97a10b053c572926f854e77bf3427abfe57",
